      "title": "In-place slice removal aliases backing array",
      "message": "The removal callback mutates p.Tokens in place with append on a sub-slice. This shifts elements in the shared backing array, so any slice previously captured from p.Tokens (for example the one a rendered View or the test's own fullLast reference) can observe shifted data. The test takes the last token by value before removal, which is safe, but in-place mutation inside a callback invoked during event dispatch is fragile.",
